## 6. Requirements

### 6.1 Functional
- Understand an open-ended travel goal from one sentence.
- Obtain the user's current location **only** via explicit device/browser permission — never assumed or inferred.
- Progressively collect only the missing information needed, one highest-value question at a time (never a long form).
- Delegate to specialist agents for transport, accommodation, activities, weather, budget, and risk.
- Produce a feasible day-by-day itinerary honoring hard constraints and scoring soft preferences.
- Independently validate every generated itinerary before it is shown.
- Replan automatically (partial, not full regeneration) on validation failure or live event.
- Support "what-if" simulations without mutating the committed plan.
- Require explicit human approval before any booking or payment.

### 6.2 Non-functional
- Deterministic arithmetic and calendar/time logic (no LLM math).
- Every specialist agent call returns a structured, confidence-scored, source-attributed contract.
- Full trace observability per trip, per agent, per tool call.
- Graceful degradation when a provider API is down or data is stale.

### 6.3 Candidate requirement fields (collected progressively, not all at once)
Starting location · destination · travel dates or flexible range · duration · traveler count (adults/children) · budget & currency · transport mode preferences · maximum transfers · preferred departure time · accommodation type & budget · food preferences · activities/interests · travel pace · must-visit places · places to avoid · accessibility needs · scenic-route preference · weather sensitivity · risk tolerance.

