## 9. Agent Responsibilities

| # | Agent | Responsibility | Never does |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Requirement Interview | NL → structured requirements: known, missing, hard constraints, soft preferences, ambiguities. Picks next highest-value question. | Doesn't guess unstated hard constraints. |
| 2 | Location | Receives device-approved coordinates, reverse-geocodes, checks accuracy/staleness, asks for confirmation. | Never accesses GPS itself. |
| 3 | Transport | Flights/trains/buses/cars/bikes/taxis/mixed — cost, duration, transfers, times, reliability, baggage, buffers. | Never invents schedules or prices. |
| 4 | Accommodation | Hotels/hostels/homestays/resorts — price, availability, location, ratings, cancellation, check-in/out. | Never hallucinates current price or availability. |
| 5 | Activities/Places | Attractions, restaurants, nature, culture, adventure, photography spots, events, hours, clustering. | Never ignores opening-hours conflicts. |
| 6 | Weather & Season | Temperature, precipitation, wind, visibility, severe-weather flags, seasonal accessibility. | Never treats weather as decorative text — it feeds itinerary re-sequencing. |
| 7 | Budget | Full category breakdown: transport, lodging, food, local transit, activities, tickets, insurance, buffer, misc. | Never performs the arithmetic itself — calls the deterministic budget service. |
| 8 | Risk & Safety | Weather risk, transport delay risk, remote-area risk, transfer-gap risk, document requirements, emergency planning. | Never gives unsupported medical advice. |
| 9 | Itinerary Planner | Synthesizes all agent outputs into one feasible day-by-day plan honoring hard/soft constraints. | Never skips the validation step. |
| 10 | Validation | Independently checks dates, times, durations, check-in windows, hours, budget, weather fit, geography, overlaps, buffers, data freshness. | Never trusts the planner's own self-report. |
| 11 | Replanning | On failure or live event: impact analysis → identify affected items → repair only those → re-validate. | Never regenerates the whole trip unnecessarily. |
| 12 | Booking | Prepares booking actions for later-stage execution. | Never books, pays, or cancels without explicit human approval. |

