## 28. Evaluation Framework

Automated benchmark across 14 scenarios: budget trip, luxury trip, family trip, solo trip, flexible dates, train-only, flight-only, weather disruption, flight delay, hotel cancellation, budget reduction, additional travel day, destination change mid-planning, provider API failure.

Metrics, with deterministic assertions wherever possible: requirement-completion rate, constraint-satisfaction rate, factual grounding (no unsupported claims), itinerary feasibility, budget accuracy (recomputed vs. reported), API efficiency (calls per completed plan), end-to-end latency, replanning success rate, recovery rate after simulated failures.

## 29. Testing

- **Unit tests** per agent, mocking tool responses to assert routing and output-contract shape.
- **Contract tests** for every MCP tool (schema in/out, error shapes).
- **Golden-path integration tests** using the 14 evaluation scenarios as fixtures.
- **Chaos tests** — inject provider timeouts and malformed responses to verify graceful degradation, not crashes.
- **Replanning regression tests** — assert that a replan touches only the expected slice of the itinerary (catches accidental full-regeneration bugs).

## 30. Deployment

- Stateless FastAPI service instances behind a load balancer; LangGraph execution state persisted in PostgreSQL/Redis so any instance can resume a trip.
- Background workers for event ingestion and long-running research fan-out.
- Feature-flagged rollout for the Booking Agent given its elevated risk profile.
- Blue/green deploys with contract-test gating before promoting a new agent version.

