## 34. End-to-End Ladakh Workflow (flagship demo)

> *"Plan a 7-day Ladakh trip in October for 2 people from my current location under ₹80,000. I prefer shorter travel and photography."*

1. Requests location permission → determines starting city.
2. Collects the few unresolved requirements (dates already implied by "October," budget and travelers already given).
3. Launches Transport, Accommodation, Activities, Weather, Budget, and Risk agents in parallel.
4. Retrieves current transport options, weather outlook, and place data.
5. Builds a candidate itinerary; the solver optimizes across cost, time, and photography-relevant clustering.
6. Validator finds an impossible schedule (a same-day transfer that doesn't allow for check-in).
7. Replanner fixes only the affected day.
8. Validator approves the revised plan.
9. Final itinerary is presented with cost/time/experience variants on a map.
10. User confirms and the trip goes live.
11. A `FLIGHT_DELAYED` event arrives mid-trip.
12. Impact analysis determines only the arrival-day activities are affected.
13. Only those items are replanned; the rest of the trip is untouched.
14. Validator re-approves; the user receives an updated itinerary.

